; ches_source runs diagnostic sources: the asynchronous side of the boundary in
; Ches_error.Source_event / Source_request. It owns timers, processes, and (from phase
; 10) the language-server session. It must not depend on ches_screen, ches_ui, bonsai,
; or any terminal library; ches_ui wires it into the UI state. Unlike ches_core,
; ches_input, ches_app, and ches_error, it may use Async. ches_core supplies the
; cell layout that turns protocol positions into display columns; lsp and jsonrpc
; (from the ocaml-lsp repository) are the protocol's types and framing only.

(library
 (name ches_source)
 (libraries ches_error ches_core core core_unix core_unix.filename_unix core_unix.sys_unix async lsp jsonrpc)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_jane)))
